Announcing ARC Prize Research Summit 2026 Keynote Speaker

Stephen Wolfram

@stephen_wolfram is the creator of Mathematica, Wolfram|Alpha, founder of Wolfram Research, and author of “A New Kind of Science,” exploring how simple rules produce complex behavior. https://t.co/g95SaDR7Hf

Taking a step back from the ups-and-downs of the oil market, one remarkable feat: global economic growth remains largely unchanged since the spring. 

@KGeorgieva: "Steady global growth has continued"

The IMF/WB annual gathering is next week: https://t.co/Rn1XhHXA5L

What happens to software when almost anyone can build it?

And what happens to the people who build it for a living?

@Replit founder and CEO @amasad will tackle both tough questions on Disrupt, and you can still get a discounted ticket to watch live: https://t.co/F4yoerOpiK https://t.co/trpynTJLK8

Can U.S. open-weight AI companies catch up to China?

@joinHandshake Director of AI Research @jomulr argues that Nvidia’s funding could be crucial—and estimates one model’s training bill, Beam, at around $100 million.

“That is not a cheap way to catch up at all.” https://t.co/c3RAg1uFVM

Anthropic is making their AI cheaper with Haiku 5.5. 

@joinHandshake Director of AI Research @jomulr explains Anthropic’s approach to cutting costs: 

“Only 5% of the time you're using this really smart Opus model. And the other 95% of the LM calls are this cheap Haiku model” https://t.co/lMHVCdy1ZL

Qualcomm’s CEO on the coming AI phone supercycle

@cristianoamon on the China vs. US AI sentiment, how AI is changing smartphones and wearables, Qualcomm’s data center strategy, and 6G.

We discuss why he thinks phones aren’t going away, how agents will use our personal context, https://t.co/0nFU1F7ZIX
